# Allowlist: Vercel receives only what the website build (vercel.mjs) needs. Everything else
# (cms/ server, fixtures and Supabase files, docs/, .env files, the committed root HTML, briefs,
# screenshots) never leaves this machine or the repository. The build reads templates/, data/ and tools/,
# imports cms/shared/ (content helpers, no secrets) and copies css/, js/ and assets/ into dist/,
# the only folder Vercel serves. Add a path here only if tools/build.mjs starts to need it.
/*
!/vercel.mjs
!/templates
!/data
/data/migration
!/tools
!/css
!/js
!/assets
!/cms
/cms/*
!/cms/shared
# The CMS Vercel project (Root Directory "cms") is built from this same repository and Vercel applies
# this file to it too. It needs its dashboard, API, build script and the seed fixture; its page preview
# imports tools/ and reads data/*.json and assets/icons (all allowed above). Never the CMS's .env files,
# local data, backups, tests or SQL. The website project still serves only dist/, so none of these
# files becomes public there.
!/cms/package.json
!/cms/vercel.json
!/cms/api
!/cms/server
!/cms/scripts
!/cms/public
!/cms/fixtures
